{
  "run_id": "PMC13270461__broad__synth_mixed_b_o3mini__s2",
  "auditor": "trapi:gpt-5.6-sol_2026-07-09",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Increasing and uniformly distributing oxidation-promoting elements such as Cr and Al in multiprincipal-element alloys promotes rapid formation of a continuous protective oxide scale at high temperature.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10384371::web::027::4_3_oxidation_in_air",
        "PMC13208696::web::025::3_6_high_temperature_oxidation_mechanism"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting oxide scale will be adherent.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC13208696::web::025::3_6_high_temperature_oxidation_mechanism",
        "PMC6317005::web::016::4_1_oxidation_kinetics_and_mechanisms"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "A continuous protective oxide scale limits oxygen ingress and further oxidation.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10384371::web::027::4_3_oxidation_in_air",
        "PMC13208696::web::025::3_6_high_temperature_oxidation_mechanism"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Limiting oxygen ingress through the protective scale preserves the alloy's mechanical integrity.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The starting material is a conventionally processed, homogeneous multiprincipal-element alloy with uniform elemental distribution and no preformed surface oxide.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Surface segregation of oxidation-promoting elements produces a continuous, coherent oxide scale in situ.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC13208696::web::025::3_6_high_temperature_oxidation_mechanism"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "A refined microstructure with high grain-boundary density can accelerate protective-scale formation.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC13208696::web::025::3_6_high_temperature_oxidation_mechanism"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Grain boundaries act as short-circuit diffusion paths for Al and Cr.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC13208696::web::025::3_6_high_temperature_oxidation_mechanism"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Greater availability of Cr and Al promotes their transport or segregation to the surface and oxidation there.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10384371::web::027::4_3_oxidation_in_air",
        "PMC13208696::web::025::3_6_high_temperature_oxidation_mechanism"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Cr- and Al-containing protective scale is self-healing.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The protective scale acts as an oxygen-diffusion barrier and slows subsequent oxidation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10384371::web::027::4_3_oxidation_in_air"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cr- and Al-enriched variants will form thinner oxide scales than the baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cr- and Al-enriched variants will form more uniform and adherent oxide scales than the baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC13208696::web::025::3_6_high_temperature_oxidation_mechanism"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cr- and Al-enriched variants will exhibit lower oxidation weight gain than the baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10384371::web::027::4_3_oxidation_in_air",
        "PMC13208696::web::025::3_6_high_temperature_oxidation_mechanism"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cr- and Al-enriched variants will retain mechanical properties better than the baseline after oxidation.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A baseline with lower concentrations of oxidation-promoting elements will develop a thicker, less continuous scale, experience greater weight gain, and suffer greater mechanical degradation.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10384371::web::027::4_3_oxidation_in_air",
        "PMC13208696::web::025::3_6_high_temperature_oxidation_mechanism"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed governing behavior should hold during sustained oxidation in air from approximately 900 to 1200 degrees Celsius.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10384371::web::027::4_3_oxidation_in_air",
        "PMC6317005::web::016::4_1_oxidation_kinetics_and_mechanisms"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Trace Y can improve scale stability and adherence through a reactive-element effect involving fine Y2O3 particles and interfacial pinning.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC13208696::web::025::3_6_high_temperature_oxidation_mechanism"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Vanadium-rich oxide formation and V2O5 evaporation can reduce scale adherence and activate breakaway oxidation at temperatures of at least 700 degrees Celsius in TiAl-based or AlNbTiVZr0.25 alloys.",
      "field": "supporting_evidence_ids",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6317005::web::016::4_1_oxidation_kinetics_and_mechanisms"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Failure of the enriched samples to show a statistically significant improvement in scale morphology, weight gain, and mechanical-property retention relative to the baseline would falsify the hypothesis.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.falsification_rule",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
